  "observations": "XXX\n[xx.xx, RT xx°C and RH xx%]\nAdd 12.5 mL of neutral alumina to a 25 mL frit funnel.\nAttach the funnel to a vacuum filter adapter and a 250 mL RBF.\nWet the alumina with THF\nLoad the reaction mixture\nElute with THF (75 mL) and weak suction. (eluate:  )  (The alumina pad became xx green at the top, xx green in the middle, and a xx brown part at the bottom.)\nAdd 25 mL of EtOH to the eluate\nConcentrate with rotovap to 25 mL (dark xx precipitation)\nCollect the solids by filtration with a filter paper (15A, ø 90 mm, tare: 0.51740 g), a glass funnel, a vacuum filter adapter, and a 100 mL RBF under suction. (filtrate: dark green solution)\nRinse with EtOH x3 and petroleum ether x2.\nDry the residue under vacuum (diaphragm pump) for 1 h. [dark brown solid]\n xxx g wt. on filter paper.\nTransfer to vial with label and tape (tare: g). -->  g\nThe residue on filter paper → 1H NMR F (CDCl3) [xxx solution]\n1H NMR P_unfiltered (CDCl3) [dark red-brown suspension] → Syringe filter → 1H NMR_P [dark xxx solution]\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nRinse the frit thoroughly or use a membrane filter\nConduct short pad chromatography together with Kenichi\nCheck NMR after chromatography\nUse reprecipitation with CHCl3/hexane\n\n\n\n\n\n\nReprecipitation procedures. Ref. BMI-109 for TAPP 1 g\n\nCHCl3 deacidification\n500 mL RBF\nBasic Al2O3\nCHCl3 170 mL (mix in flask ---> then filter)\nFritted funnel (por.4), suction adapter (60 mbar, full open), 50 mL wide-neck RBF (blow-cleaned)\nFiltered\n\nReprecipitation\nPurified CHCl3 100 mL, sonicate\n-> 100 µL + CDCl3 500 µL -> NMR1\nn-hexane 550 mL, manually stir, sonicate\nFridge, (30 min)\nGlass Funnel, Filter paper (big, 15A), suction adapter (60 mbar), 1000 mL wide-neck RBF\nFilter w/ fully open suction\nTransfer & rinse w/ 2 x (purified CHCl3 5 mL + 25 mL hex), closed suction\nRinse w/ hex x2, closed suction (2x25mL)\nDry w/ fully open suction (15 mbar), vacuum o/n\n20 mL vial, PTFE sealing (tare w/ lid: _______ g)\n→ _____ mg product\n-> Weight, NMR2 (CDCl3, DMSO)\n",
